cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "station-archive: a reconciled daily station-observation archive builder"
message: >-
  If you use this software, or an archive built with it, please cite it.
  When you cite an archive rather than the code, also cite the provenance
  record the archive carries (manifests/provenance.json), which names the
  policy and the provider releases that produced it.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Giorgos
    family-names: Ntagkounakis
    email: giorgosntagkounakis@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-2041-6939"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gntag/station-archive"
abstract: >-
  station-archive reconciles several overlapping public climate sources --
  ECA&D, GHCN-Daily, NOAA GSOD and the Copernicus C3S land collection -- into a
  single daily station-observation archive in which every accepted value has one
  physical-station identity, one chosen source, a recorded reason for that
  choice, and a traceable path back to the provider record it came from.

  Rather than concatenating sources, it resolves station identity on series
  evidence, rejects values the providers themselves document as
  non-observations, selects one value per station-date-variable by a per-variable
  source priority, and refuses to splice a source switch that fails a bias,
  dispersion, wet-day-frequency and monthly-discontinuity test -- leaving the gap
  open instead. Breakpoints are diagnosed by relative homogeneity testing and
  flagged; no value is ever altered.
keywords:
  - climate data
  - station observations
  - data provenance
  - duplicate detection
  - homogeneity testing
  - quality control
